Z||000000||sbecher||12-03-2000||11:20 PM||||Hi all,<BR>This is my first post here.  I was hanging out with a friend of mine this weekend, and we worked on his Fiero a little bit.  Then he was telling me about all the different stuff you can do with Fieros.  Basically, he got me hooked on the car.  Anyways, I was wondering what kinds of problems people have had with their Fieros?  I might be getting one, so I just want a little background info.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Shawn Becher||||reg||5
Z||000001||Hank is Here||12-03-2000||11:28 PM||||I must say that the Fiero is like any other car, look for normal wear points.  Do the engine tranny, steering and brakes work correct?  Has it been in an accident?   Look for rust, yes Fiero's do rust in their unibody construction (especially look under the truck carpet).  My Fiero has been rather problem free for me over the past 10 months or so with nickle and dime stuff ( my guess adding up to less than $200), temp sending unit, headlight motor, headliner and that is it. I feel since my car was well maintained before I had it maintiance is well below average for a 13 year old car.   <P>Also welcome to the forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||12-03-2000||11:38 PM||||Welcome!!! Hank is right, it's just like any other 13yr old car. I bought mine with 67,000<BR>on the meter,it was very well taken care of.I have had very few problems with it and I also take very good care of it. Just stay with us there's lots of info here.<P>Go here:  <A HREF="http://www.fierproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierproject.com</A>    Lots of info and some good fiero links can be found here<P><BR>DXR_DAD<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||12-03-2000||11:48 PM||||don't get a fiero. they suck. (no flames)<BR>just kiddin.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>even though i've had quite a few problems that p!ss me off, and my car still isn't running, i still like 'em.<BR>newayz...yeah look for the normal stuff like any other car.  check to see who owned it if possible.  (by the way, if a male teenager has owned it, it doesn't mean it was driven hard or anything)  miles aren't a big factor, i think there was some1 on here that had over 300K miles on their fiero!<BR>any yes, there are many things you can do with a fiero.  more than i've seen with any car.<BR>by the way, welcome to the forum.<BR>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>fiero7@hotmail.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||12-04-2000||12:02 AM||||You'll find some answers here, among other places.  This is just one of the most recent threads discussing reliability...<BR>-  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004466.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004466.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||12-04-2000||12:10 AM||||To make a point, don't listen to Sqoach..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Miles ARE a big factor. Even if the engine still runs good, the rest of the car has 300k on it...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Male teenagers usually don't drive hard (me included) but our minds slip, and we let the car rev to redline.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Also, check for rust on the engine cradle.. trust me on that one.||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||12-04-2000||12:49 AM||||My best Fiero's came from women. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DrRodey||12-04-2000||01:02 PM||||Hey Shawn...  Thanks for the help this weekend.. Glad to see you are starting to see the light...<P>You Know everythign i've told you.. just listen to these guys.. they know whats going on.  I've taken some good info fro them and Hope you enjoy thmeas much as i have.   <P>Welcome and make yourself athome..<P>------------------<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTABLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/files/fieroPage.JPG">     <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A>||||reg||1
